<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Potomac-Blues.jpg" alt="A plein air painting with a figure. Extra painting and scumbling done back in the studio" width="450" height="323" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Potomac Blues. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2014.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Sometimes paintings don't turn out too well and after looking at them in the studio for a few weeks I will often play around with the painting to try out new techniques and approaches.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This is a plein air painting done at Riverside Potomac that I revisited to add new layers via scumbling and glazing. &nbsp;My goals were to increase the feeling of soft light and bring a feeling of mood by playing on the blue/orange/green colors. I also placed a figure in the painting to give it a strong center of interest.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">You can see the original version of the painting here:&nbsp;<a href="http://www.portraitsbysimonbland.com/blog/post/painting-on-location-riverside-at-the-potomac">http://www.portraitsbysimonbland.com/blog/post/painting-on-location-riverside-at-the-potomac</a></p>